      "message": "[Gerrit AI Review] ❌ **Changes Requested**\n\n`data-\u003eall_protected` acts as an absolute software lock that rejects writes to the entire flash. However, `get_protect` omits this check and only evaluates the status register coverage (`flash_check_prot_reg`).\n\nThis creates a state inconsistency: if a bank falls outside the status register range but `all_protected \u003d\u003d true`, `get_protect` incorrectly reports `0` (writable), even though a `write` call to that bank will be rejected with `EC_ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED`.\n\nReturn `1` when `all_protected` is enabled:\n```c\n\tif (data-\u003eall_protected) {\n\t\treturn 1;\n\t}\n\n\tif (flash_check_prot_reg(dev, addr_start, CONFIG_FLASH_BANK_SIZE) \u003d\u003d\n\t    EC_ERROR_ACCESS_DENIED) {\n\t\treturn 1;\n\t}\n```\n[🔗](http://go/tj/e7e3ee12-8177-4718-aeb4-84841200af5b)",
